New finding
P1-1 NOT CLOSED — docs/spec/SESSION_HANDLE_PROFILE_V1.md:137-147 orders admission, workspace, epoch, budget, then head-bound root. In code, crates/sley-protocol/src/server.rs:609-615 invokes session_check before testing budget; crates/sley-protocol/src/session.rs:427-439 performs the head-bound root comparison within session_check. Thus an exhausted session with an advanced root receives SESSION_ROOT_ADVANCED before PROTOCOL_LIMIT_EXCEEDED, contrary to contract item 5 before item 6. The existing evidence only exercises workspace mismatch versus exhausted budget (crates/sley-protocol/src/server_tests.rs:1448-1468), not root mismatch versus exhausted budget. scripts/check_session_handle_profile.py checks tables and markers but not this call-order relationship.

